cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use modeltrees, please cite the software and the publications
  whose methods it implements: Zeileis, Hothorn and Hornik (2008) for
  model-based recursive partitioning, and Rusch (2012) when you use the
  negative binomial model.
title: modeltrees
abstract: >-
  Model-based recursive partitioning (MOB) in Python, ported from R's
  partykit, with negative binomial, safe logit and multinomial node models.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
authors:
  - alias: BNM
